    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the complement of the 42-degree angle:**\n   The complement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 90 degrees. Therefore, we calculate the complement of 42 degrees as follows:\n   \\[\n   90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ\n   \\]\n   So, the complement of a 42-degree angle is 48 degrees.\n\n2. **Determine the supplement of the 48-degree angle:**\n   The supplement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, equals 180 degrees. Therefore, we calculate the supplement of 48 degrees as follows:\n   \\[\n   180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ\n   \\]\n   So, the supplement of a 48-degree angle is 132 degrees.\n\nThus, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \\(\\boxed{132}\\).",
