      "sample_index": 5,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle. Let's break this down step by step.\n\n1. **Find the complement of the 42-degree angle:**\n   The complement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, gives 90 degrees. Therefore, the complement of a 42-degree angle is:\n   \\[\n   90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the supplement of the 48-degree angle:**\n   The supplement of an angle is what, when added to the angle, gives 180 degrees. Therefore, the supplement of a 48-degree angle is:\n   \\[\n   180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nSo, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \\(\\boxed{132}\\).",
